tent="1-143692">Learn more about Westminster Green Investment</div><div data-ai-no-open-words="" data-content="1-143693">The second phase of Westminster Green Investment closed in March 2026, taking the total they have raised to £3 million. The next phase of investment will be launching soon, sign up for updates to get more news.</div><div data-ai-no-open-button-text="" data-content="1-143694">Sign up for updates</div><div data-ai-no-open-button-url="" data-content="1-143695">/signup-for-updates</div><div data-ai-no-past-invest-header="" data-content="1-143696">Placeholder</div><div data-ai-no-past-invest-copy="" data-content="1-143697">placeholder</div><div data-ai-no-past-invest-button-url="" data-content="1-143698">/</div><div data-ai-no-past-invest-button-text="" data-content="1-143699">Learn more</div><div data-ai-no-chart-img-url="" data-content="1-143700">https://cdn4.sharein.com/abundance/cms/fd81e4f6-d21a-4e91-84fd-4b7e41b130f2.jpg</div><div data-ai-no-chart-img-alt="" data-content="1-143701">An image of a greening project</div><div data-ai-no-chart-img-caption="" data-content="2-143702">The council has been investing in greening projects across the borough</div></div><section class="position-relative bg-colour--primary-surface p-t-spacer-4xl type-white ai-hero" style="background:#06326e"><div class="container"><div class="row brand-media-box align-items-start"><div class="col-12 col-md-8"><h1 class="text-choke-md--640 text-center--md font-secondary" style="color:#fff" data-content="1-143703">Westminster City Council</h1><p class="body--xl text-choke-md--640 text-center--md m-b-spacer-sm" style="color:#fff" data-content="2-143707">Westminster Council wants to create a net zero city by 2040 by backing green projects across their community.</p></div><div class="col-12 col-md-4"><div class="ai-heroLogoRail"><img class="image-responsive hero-header__illustration brand-media-box__img" src="https://cdn4.sharein.com/abundance/cms/ee615523-c331-4e2d-985d-b4475979e79c.png" alt="Westminster Council logo" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high"></div></div></div></div></section><div class="bg-colour--primary-surface bg-mask bg-mask--b-convex m-b-spacer-2xl ai-hero-mask" style="background:#06326e"></div><div id="ai-scope-wrap"><section class="m-b-spacer-lg ai-scope"><div class="container text-choke-960"><div class="row"><div class="col-12 text-center" data-content="2-143712"><p class="body--xl">Westminster City Council is committed to tackling climate change and aims to become a net zero city by 2040. After declaring a climate emergency in 2019, the council has already taken significant steps to cut its own emissions and is now helping residents and local businesses make a positive impact in their neighbourhoods, reducing carbon footprints and improving the local environment. <br><br>Westminster has some of the highest carbon emissions in the country. To reach its goal of becoming a net zero council by 2030, Westminster needs to find ways to reduce city-wide emissions by 91,000 tonnes a year. To make this possible, Westminster Green Investment was launched to help fund projects that will create a cleaner, greener and fairer Westminster for everyone.</p></div></div></div></section><div class="bg-colour--primary-surface bg-mask bg-mask--t-convex ai-no-open-mask ai-scope" style="background-color: rgb(255, 237, 204);"></div><section class="home-green-investing position-relative p-y-spacer-xs bg-colour--primary-surface ai-no-open ai-scope" style="background-color: rgb(255, 237, 204);"><div class="container"><div class="row"><div class="col-12"><div class="flex-center"><h2 class="text-center m-b-spacer-sm">Learn more about Westminster Green Investment</h2></div><div class="flex-center"><p class="body--lg text-center choke-800 m-b-spacer-sm">The second phase of Westminster Green Investment closed in March 2026, taking the total they have raised to £3 million. The next phase of investment will be launching soon, sign up for updates to get m